## WHAT ACTUALLY BLOCKED IT

**THE SUCCESSOR STEP, AND ITS PUBLISHED DIAGNOSIS IS WRONG.**
`[LJ-1.536]` attributes that row's cost to two spellings of a finite successor
tower: "98 PERCENT OF THE COST IS `sucV`"
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md:248`), measured in files that import
no hierarchy chapter (`runs/Control536e.agda`, `runs/Control536f.agda`).

**THAT COST IS REAL AND IT IS CURABLE, AND CURING IT BUYS NOTHING.** Prove the
step identity at a VARIABLE `n` and `step` is stuck at every row, so `sucV` is
never unfolded: `runs/Control565a.agda` is that task's `Control536e.agda` with
one line changed and costs **0.84 s** (`runs/ctla-0.time`) against its 425.73 s.
Spending that cure at the real successor step still exhausts **11.05 GB**
(`runs/Control565b.agda`, `runs/ctlb-0.time`). **A measured cure does not
transfer by analogy (`AGENTS.md:45`); I re-measured it at its own site and there
it failed.**

**THE REAL CAUSE IS THE `isL` WITNESS, AND FIVE CONTROLS BRACKET IT.**

| file | what it asks | result |
|---|---|---|
| `runs/Control565d.agda` | `HierBelow` at a successor FORMED, no proof | exit 0, **1.93 s** |
| `runs/Control565e.agda` | `hierL (sucV α) h o` against itself, `h` `o` abstract | exit 0, **1.44 s** |
| `runs/Control565c.agda` | `HierBelow (sucV α) (suc-ord oα)` against the same set spelled the other way, **no stage move at all** | **HEAP WALL, 11.05 GB, 263.63 s** |
| `runs/Control565f.agda` | the same, with the second name written out locally | **HEAP WALL, 10.94 GB, 240.56 s** |
| `runs/Control565g.agda` | (c) with the witness a PARAMETER, nothing else changed | exit 0, **1.93 s** |

**(c) AND (g) ARE THE CONTROLLED PAIR AND THE VARIABLE IS THE WITNESS.**
`HierBelow` computes it (`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/Probe536.agda:186-187` through
`:135-136`), and `isL-ord` bottoms out in `ord∈Lset-suc`, which is
`∈-induction` (`src/L/Ordinal/Stages.lagda.md:434-435`) applied to a TRANSPARENT
`sucV α`. **(c) also refutes the `sucV`-spelling diagnosis on its own**: it
spells the stage the same way on both sides and walls anyway.

**I DID NOT READ THE MECHANISM OUT OF AGDA AND I DO NOT ASSERT IT.** What is
measured is the differential. The sentence above about `ord∈Lset-suc` is the
best explanation I have for it and it is an inference.

