## WHAT IS DELIVERED

`agents/tasks/LJ-1-565/Probe565.agda`, 368 lines, 105 non-blank non-comment.

### The successor step, which three attempts could not write

`Probe565.agda:212-219`, exit 0 at **27.37 s** measured alone
(`runs/Control565h.agda`, `runs/ctlh-0.time`).

`[LJ-1.536]` states it in a comment and prices it above the caliber
(`Probe536.agda:370-393`). **Attempt 1 built four routes to it and every one
walled** (`runs/attempt-1-review-of-stage-high.md.preserved`, `## What blocks
it, measured`): through `[LJ-1.536]`'s `seq`, through the chapter's uniqueness
law, through a fresh instantiation of that task's engine, and through that
instantiation with its own cure. **Every one of the four targets
`HierBelow (sucV α) (suc-ord oα)`, whose witness is computed at a transparent
successor.** This row targets the witness-abstract statement instead, and it
spends BOTH cures: the stage by `step-suc` (`:140-142`), the witness by
`hierL-irr` (`:188-193`), which is the chapter's uniqueness law
(`src/L/Hierarchy.lagda.md:507-508`) used as a PATH and never as a conversion.

### And it composes, which is the half that matters

`Probe565.agda:232-234`, exit 0 at **1.95 s** (`runs/Control565w.agda`,
`runs/ctlw-0.time`).

A green row in a weaker statement is worth nothing if the wall only moves to
where the witness must be supplied. **It does not.** The witness is a redex only
when its argument is a transparent successor; at a VARIABLE γ it is stuck, so
`bridge` is `refl` and `allH→all` (`:242-243`) carries the whole class back to
`[LJ-1.536]`'s own statement for free.

### The induction, and the transport that walled twice

`Probe565.agda:289-309`, exit 0 at **24.34 s** (`runs/Control565x.agda`,
`runs/ctlx-0.time`).

Attempt 1's `MoveAlong` carries the obligation along `sucV δ ≡ γ` and walled at
8 GB in two independent forms, a `PathP` from `isProp→PathP` (`runs/ctls-0.out`)
and the uniqueness law (`runs/ctlt-0.out`). **Here that step is gone rather than
cured:** `Motive` (`:236-237`) quantifies over both witnesses, so moving it
along the equation is a plain `subst` on a motive that never names a computed
witness. No `PathP`, no uniqueness law, no case analysis at that point.

### The ordinal split, which is attempt 1's

`Probe565.agda:259-268`, free at 1.84 s (`runs/Control565v.agda`,
`runs/ctlv-0.out`). **The credit is attempt 1's and I restate its rows only
because a control is not a module to import a `where` block from.** `suc∈or≡`
(`src/L/Ordinal/Stages.lagda.md:137-139`) says a member's successor either stays
inside the ordinal or IS it, so refusing an immediate predecessor is exactly
`[LJ-1.519]`'s `IsLimit`. **Zero needs no case of its own**, because `IsLimit ∅`
holds with nothing to prove.

### The obligation's conditional form

`Probe565.agda:327-328`. `reduction` is `[LJ-1.536]`'s green route from
`HierBelowAll` to `StageHigh`, imported and not restated.

## WHAT IS LEFT

**`HierBelowLimitH` (`Probe565.agda:285-287`), AND NOTHING ELSE.**

At a limit γ the members of `hierL γ` are the pairs `pr c (Lset c)` for c ∈ γ.
To carve that set out of a stage the formula must say "w is the tower's value at
c" INSIDE the stage, and that is the level formula: `Σ₁`, with the existential
over an approximation UNBOUNDED at the ambient level
(`dev/literature/devlin-II5.md:217`). The stage's own satisfaction is what
bounds it (`:221-222`, "witnessed inside the carrier").

**THE BRIEF ORDERS THE STOP HERE AND I TAKE IT.** "IF THE REAL BLOCKER IS AN
UNBOUNDED SEARCH, SAY SO AND STOP. `[LJ-1.560]` is running on exactly that
question and this brief must not duplicate it."

**AND THE BRIEF'S SECOND PRIZE IS ONLY HALF EARNED, WHICH I SAY PLAINLY.** It
offers: "A NO-GO THAT NAMES AN UNBOUNDED SEARCH CONFIRMS THE SHARED WALL FROM A
SECOND SITE." **This task did not reach the limit case and measured nothing
about it**, exactly as attempt 1 said of itself. The identification of the limit
case with `[LJ-1.560]`'s question is an argument from the two literature lines
above plus `agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md`'s `## FOR THE NEXT BRIEF`
point 2. **It is not a measurement, and `stage-high-from-limit` does not depend
on it.** A second site by argument is worth less than a second site by
measurement and I do not price it as the latter.

## THE WALL

**FOUR HEAP EXHAUSTIONS AT THE WIDE CALIBER, AND NOT ONE WAS RERUN.**
`GHCRTS="-A64m -I0 -M8g"` on the pane, set by the program and untouched. One
Agda process per run.

| file | seconds | peak RSS | what it was |
|---|---|---|---|
| `runs/Control565b.agda` | 268.12 | 11.05 GB | the successor step with the step cure alone |
| `runs/Control565c.agda` | 263.63 | 11.05 GB | the type identity, no stage move |
| `runs/Control565f.agda` | 240.56 | 10.94 GB | the same with the name written out |

The fourth is attempt 1's `runs/ctlb-0` at 239.81 s, recorded in
`runs/accept-1.out`; my `Control565b.agda` reproduces it independently at the
same file name, which is how I first learned the two attempts had met the same
wall.

**A NOTE ON THE CALIBER.** `-M8g` is the GHC heap cap and the peak RSS above is
about 11 GB, so the process holds more resident than the cap it is refusing to
exceed. I report both numbers as measured and I do not reconcile them.

## THE PROPOSED LAW

`[LJ-1.536]` proposed "Spell a finite successor tower ONE way". **That law is
true and it is not the one that matters here**, and its own site is now the
counter-example: `runs/Control565c.agda` spells the tower one way and walls.

I propose this instead, and I do not write it into `dev/LESSONS.md`, which is
not in this task's scope:

> **Hold a proof witness ABSTRACT when its argument is transparent.** A
> statement that COMPUTES an `isL` or an `IsOrd` witness at `sucV α` puts a
> well-founded recursion over a transparent term into every conversion that
> touches it. Take the witness as a parameter, carry it abstract through the
> whole induction, and supply it once at a VARIABLE, where nothing unfolds. It
> costs nothing to do: the value does not depend on the witness, and the
> chapter's own uniqueness law moves between two of them by a PATH. Measured
> 2026-08-23 at `[LJ-1.565]`: 11.05 GB against 1.93 s, one variable, at
> `runs/Control565c.agda` and `runs/Control565g.agda`.

**THIS IS LAW P-l'S SHAPE AT A NEW PLACE.** P-l (`dev/LESSONS.md:2357`) says a
statement may be about a concrete stage without dragging that stage's
PRESENTATION into its type. This says the same about a PROOF: a statement may be
about a concrete ordinal without dragging the CONSTRUCTION of its witness into
the terms that get converted. **P-l's own clause says a measured cure does not
transfer by analogy, so this was measured here and not inherited.**

## C-42, THE SWEEP

C-42 (`dev/LESSONS.md:3752`) says a refutation measures ONE site and never how
far the shape extends, so the count comes before the cure. **What is refuted
here is a published DIAGNOSIS, not a statement**, so the sweep counts the shape
the diagnosis mispriced: a proof witness COMPUTED at a transparent successor.

| shape | count | evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `Lset→isL (sucV …)` in `src/` | **4**, across 4 files | `L/Cardinal.lagda.md:73`, `L/SquareLawClosed.lagda.md:52`, `L/Choice/Order.lagda.md:687`, `L/Axioms/Basic.lagda.md:99` |
| `isL-ord (sucV …)` in `.agda` files under `agents/tasks/` | **18** | `grep -rln "isL-ord (sucV" agents/tasks/`, `.agda` only |
| of those 18, files NOT belonging to `[LJ-1.536]` or `[LJ-1.565]` | **1** | `agents/tasks/LJ-1-521/Probe521.agda` |
| `hierL` applied to a transparent `sucV` in `src/` | **0** | `grep -rn "hierL (sucV" src/` |

**THE SHAPE IS IN `src/` AND THE DEFECT IS NOT, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE
POINT.** All four `src/` sites PRODUCE a witness and none of them converts one
against a second spelling of the same set, which is what the pair
`runs/Control565c.agda` and `runs/Control565g.agda` measures. `L/Cardinal
.lagda.md:73` is the closest, because its argument is `sucV (sucV (fst α))`.
**I did not measure any of the four and I do not claim any of them is slow.**

**SO NO CURE IS PRICED AGAINST `src/` AND NONE IS PROPOSED.** The count says
where a future conversion would be expensive, not where one is. What the
measurement binds is the next probe that states an induction over ordinals, and
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-521/Probe521.agda` is the one existing probe outside this
leg that carries the shape and would be worth a reader's eye.

